## Failure localization

- Yaw error above 1 degree: 19, 39, and 35 windows by increasing horizon.
- Every such window crosses transition 46; no other window exceeds 1 degree.
- Maximum yaw error in non-crossing windows: 2.21e-5, 1.79e-5, and 1.81e-5 degrees.
- Maximum yaw-rate error in non-crossing windows stays below 9.67e-5 deg/s.

Therefore the angular tail is caused by the identified exact-opposite quaternion/preprocessing edge,
not general free-space drift. Translation remains micro-numerically faithful throughout.

